# EtStepIndicator - Agent Guide

> **AI Assistant Documentation**: This guide helps AI coding assistants understand and work with the EtStepIndicator component.

## Overview

`EtStepIndicator` renders a horizontal step/progress indicator: a thin track with a dot per step and a label under each dot. The filled portion of the track (and every dot it reaches) is tinted in the fill color; the active step gets a larger dot and an emphasized (semibold) label. Designed for onboarding flows (Profile → Verification → Deposit) but fully generic.

## Key Architecture

- **Measured track**: the track spans from the first dot center to the last dot center. Dot centers are measured via `onLayout` on each step column, so the geometry adapts to any label widths — nothing is hardcoded.
- **Piecewise fill**: dots are positioned by their label columns and are therefore NOT evenly spaced along the track. The fill width is interpolated between the two surrounding measured dot centers (`progress * (steps - 1)` in "step units"), so integer step positions land exactly on their dots — never short of or past one.
- **Layout per Figma**: the first step column is start-aligned (dot above the label start); all other columns center the dot above the label. Columns are spread with `justifyContent: 'space-between'`.
- **Animated fill**: fill-width changes slide with an ease-out `withTiming` (reanimated). The first measured frame snaps so mounting shows no unwanted slide.
- **Theme integration**: defaults come from `useEtoroTheme` and every color is overridable via props.
- **Memoized**: main component and the `StepIndicatorStep` subcomponent use `React.memo`.

